// What the dead left behind, and what the drowned kingdom's history
// reads like carved into a wall. `src/writings.rs` loads this once; its
// lines are drawn the first time the place that holds them is entered,
// and a line already given out this run is never given out again.
//
// Every field:
//   last_words:   lines a dead adventurer scratched beside where they
//                 fell, read off a "scratched words" prop beside
//                 remains: `assets/prefabs/flavor/last_words.ron`,
//                 `assets/prefabs/reward/a_fallen_adventurer.ron` and
//                 `assets/prefabs/risk/the_last_stand.ron` each carry
//                 one. Never the same line twice a run; a run that asks
//                 for more than this file holds repeats rather than
//                 failing, which thirty-odd lines against four pieces
//                 (two "Last Words" at most, one each of the others)
//                 never does.
//   inscriptions: lines of the drowned kingdom's history, read off a
//                 "chronicle" or a "wall inscription" prop:
//                 `assets/prefabs/reward/library_nook.ron`'s book and
//                 `decor::WallInscriptions`'s own carving. Never the
//                 same line twice a run, by the same rule.
//   feelings:     [(prop:, says:)], a prop whose presence on a floor is
//                 said once, on the arrival that finds the floor,
//                 since what it is tells of what the floor holds
//                 before anyone has found it. One row for each risk
//                 piece this is worth spoiling ahead of time for: "The
//                 Flooding Vault" (`iron grate`), "The Tinder Room"
//                 (`ember plate`), "The Bone Circle" (`circle bones`),
//                 "The Warded Hall" (`warding glyph`), "The Paralysis
//                 Vestibule" (`paralysis vent`). A prop the game lays itself
//                 at build, as the sealed vault's lever, is no piece's
//                 slot and cannot be named here. The rest keep their tell for the
//                 door `assets/prefabs/risk/`'s own comment already
//                 promises, and say nothing before it.
(
    last_words: [
        "\"the water was rising. tell Mira I went down for the ring\"",
        "\"do not lift it\"",
        "\"three of us came down. I am the one left to write it\"",
        "\"they sleep in the dark beyond. walk soft\"",
        "\"the key was never on this floor. it was never on this floor\"",
        "\"Mereholt, I am sorry\"",
        "\"I can hear the bell from here, under all this water. I did not think I would\"",
        "\"my lantern went out on the stair above. I kept walking anyway\"",
        "\"whoever reads this, go back. there is nothing down here worth your name\"",
        "\"the map was wrong about this room. it is wrong about the next one too\"",
        "\"I traded the rope for the rest of the bread. I would do it again\"",
        "\"something in the dark already knew my name before I said it\"",
        "\"we drew lots for who went first through the door. I lost twice\"",
        "\"the gold is real. so is what is guarding it. I know that now\"",
        "\"I left a line of chalk behind me the whole way down. it did not help\"",
        "\"tell the town the bell still rings, down here, on its own\"",
        "\"I thought the quiet meant we were alone\"",
        "\"my own torch lit the thing's eyes before it lit anything else\"",
    ],
    inscriptions: [
        "In the reign of the last King the mere rose a hand's breadth every spring, and no prayer turned it back.",
        "The Abbess held that the cathedral's bells would keep the water out. They rang until the ropes rotted.",
        "The forges at the bottom of the world were never the king's. They were lit before there was a king, and the kingdom only learned to be afraid of them.",
        "The standing stones on the shore were raised to keep something in, the chronicle says, and not out.",
        "The King did not drown. He waited on his throne, and the water came to him.",
        "Within a generation of the flood the goblins held the upper halls, and called them a kingdom of their own.",
        "The miners struck water a hundred years before the lake ever rose, and sealed the seam, and said nothing.",
        "Every well in the old town once ran sweet. The last of them turned before the flood did, which nobody read as a warning until after.",
        "The library moved its lowest shelves twice in one generation, each time further from a floor that kept rising on its own.",
        "A census taken the year before the flood counted every soul in the lower wards twice, as if the clerks already knew only the count would be left of them.",
        "The spider that holds the warrens now is not the first to have made a home of a drowned kingdom's cellars, only the one that stayed.",
        "The old town was raised on the palace once the palace was old, as the palace had been raised on the tombs and the mines, and they on whatever was already there. Each age built over the last and called it the ground.",
        "The masons of the palace cut their cellars down until the lake wept through the walls, and went no further. They said the stone below was not theirs to cut.",
        "A people lived on the shore before the kingdom, and kept a fire that never went out. They are not in the chronicles. The chroniclers did not ask who had lit the hearths they found.",
        "Under the foundations the water is older than any wall, and does not remember the kingdom at all.",
        "What the Drowned King asked of his knights at the end was not to win, the stone in the throne room says, only to keep him company.",
    ],
    feelings: [
        (prop: "iron grate", says: "You hear water pouring somewhere below."),
        (prop: "ember plate", says: "The air smells of old smoke."),
        (prop: "circle bones", says: "The quiet here does not feel entirely empty."),
        (prop: "warding glyph", says: "Something underfoot remembers being woken, and has not forgotten."),
        (prop: "paralysis vent", says: "The air sits strangely still, like a held breath."),
    ],
)
